      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "carryover_21",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "set_variable",
            name: "carryover_percentage",
            value: 40,
          },
          {
            tag: "set_variable",
            name: "carryover_bonus",
            value: "yes",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_22",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("With the arrival of the Great Horde, and the humans having retreated, the united orcish forces held a council of war."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_23",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("After a fair amount of squabbling — for some of the older warlords were reluctant to let this young upstart lead them — and a few consequent executions, leadership of the horde was formally bestowed upon Kapou’e."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_24",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Riders were dispatched in all directions to gather intelligence and to pinpoint the exact locations of hostile forces."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_25",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("The horde was then split into two forces. On the advice of the shamans, Kapou’e placed one force under the leadership of Shan Taum the Smug, who — despite his obnoxious nature — was a fierce and capable leader. He was sent to Bitok, the most southwestern orcish city, to cut off the humans already invading the port city of Tirigaz, and to stop any further human incursion into orcish territory."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_26",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Kapou’e sent the shamans, Pirk, Gork and Vraurk back to Borstep — a city just north of the Mourned Hills — to organize any remaining orcish forces as well as create an arms and supply depot."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_27",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Kapou’e himself — desiring to settle this business once and for all — led his remaining forces to Dorest, the human city due southeast of Prestim, to which Earl Lanbec’h had retreated."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "loyal_28",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:make_loyal",
            units: "Kapou_e,Al_Brock,Flar_Tar,Arthain,Hanak",
